
 VNX-SEC-001  ● CRITICAL  AWS access key ID
 secrets · 1 credential in 3 places · committed 41 days ago · CWE-798

 WHY IT MATTERS
   An AWS access key ID (AKIA prefix) was found in source code.

 WHAT TO DO, IN THIS ORDER
   1  Revoke the credential at the provider. Deleting the line does not revoke it.
   2  Check the provider's access logs from 2026-09-03 on: a1b2c3d committed it then.
   3  Issue a replacement into your secrets manager or CI secret store.
   4  Remove it from the 3 places below. Once it is revoked, rewriting history is optional.
   more https://example.invalid/vnx-sec-001

